# YOUR MOVE — environment variables
#
# Your Move runs against its OWN Supabase project. None of these names collide with
# The Signal's, and nothing in lib/aw or lib/yourmove can reach that project.
#
# Copy these lines into the SAME .env.local you already use (or into Vercel's project
# settings). Do not commit real values, and do not paste the service-role key into chat,
# an issue, or a PR — it bypasses row-level security completely.

# --- Supabase (the new Your Move project) ---
# Project Settings → Data API → Project URL
YOURMOVE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Project Settings → API Keys → anon / public
YOURMOVE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Project Settings → API Keys → service_role. SERVER ONLY. Never expose to a browser.
YOURMOVE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE=

# The browser only needs these if a later phase subscribes to Realtime. V1A does not.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YOURMOVE_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YOURMOVE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- The facilitator console ---
# Guards /yourmove/console — the only surface that can apply the twelve-measurement
# leadership overlay. If this is unset the console stays shut rather than open.
YOURMOVE_CONSOLE_SECRET=

# --- Models (optional) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is shared with the rest of the repo. Without it, Your Move still runs:
# stage 1 falls back to the deterministic parser and stage 5 to the deterministic
# renderer. The rules are identical either way; only the prose changes.
# YOURMOVE_INTENT_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# YOURMOVE_NARRATOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
